1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,370
Listen. Practice. Speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:20,360
Good morning. Thanks for joining. Today, I want to deep dive into the upcoming product launch campaign.

3
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:30,360
I want us to cover strategy, content, channels, timeline, risks, and KPIs. The goal is full clarity before we start execution.

4
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,760
Good morning.

5
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:32,760
Sounds good.

6
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:37,760
I've reviewed the preliminary campaign brief, and I have notes on messaging, social strategy

7
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:39,560
and content gaps.

8
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:42,600
Let's go through it step by step so nothing gets missed.

9
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:43,600
Great.

10
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,920
Let's start with the campaign objective.

11
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:52,200
The main goal is to drive awareness and generate qualified leads for the new product.

12
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:57,080
Secondary goals include brand positioning, demonstrating innovation, and educating our

13
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:58,680
target audience.

14
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,080
Right.

15
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:04,280
Business and lead generation are primary, but we also need engagement metrics because

16
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:09,000
social proof and shares will extend reach beyond our immediate audience.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,240
Exactly.

18
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:13,360
For messaging, I suggest three main themes.

19
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:18,680
First, the unique product benefits, what differentiates us from competitors.

20
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:25,080
Second, customer impact stories, real examples of how the product solves problems.

21
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:26,700
Third, urgency.

22
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:30,420
Limited time offers or early access incentives.

23
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:31,100
Agreed.

24
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,820
We should also weave in brand values subtly.

25
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:37,020
Innovation, trustworthiness, and simplicity.

26
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:40,460
Every piece of content should reinforce these values.

27
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:41,100
Yes.

28
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,020
Consistency is key.

29
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,820
Now about channels.

30
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:48,220
We're looking at email, social media, LinkedIn,

31
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:51,900
Instagram, Twitter, paid ads, blog posts,

32
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:54,220
webinars, and PR outreach.

33
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:56,660
Do you see any gaps in coverage?

34
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:59,260
I think that covers the major touch points.

35
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:03,100
One addition could be video content for social and the website.

36
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:07,740
Short explainer videos or demo clips tend to boost engagement, especially on Instagram

37
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,100
and LinkedIn.

38
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,100
Good point.

39
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:13,180
We should plan at least three short videos.

40
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:18,460
One product demo, one customer testimonial, and one feature highlight.

41
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:19,460
Sounds good.

42
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:23,180
Regarding content, do we have a clear owner for each type?

43
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:31,180
Yes. I propose the following. I own email campaigns and blog posts, including SEO optimization.

44
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:38,180
You own social media, paid ads, and video coordination. PR outreach will be joint ownership.

45
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:44,180
Agreed. For social media, I'll create posts, stories, and LinkedIn articles aligned with the campaign themes.

46
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:50,180
Paid campaigns will require daily monitoring to optimize engagement and CPC.

47
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:54,180
For email, I'm planning a three-email sequence.

48
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:58,180
Announcement, feature focus, and final reminder.

49
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:01,180
Each will be tailored for different audience segments.

50
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:06,180
Existing customers, leads in the nurture pipeline, and cold prospects.

51
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,180
That segmentation is essential.

52
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:11,180
We want to avoid a one-size-fits-all approach.

53
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:14,180
Subject lines and content must vary by audience.

54
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:16,180
Exactly.

55
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:23,100
For blogs, we'll publish two long-form articles covering product benefits and use cases, plus

56
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:29,580
three supporting posts about industry trends, customer success stories, and best practices.

57
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:30,580
Make sense.

58
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,400
Don't forget SEO alignment.

59
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:37,220
We need keyword mapping before drafting, meta descriptions, and internal linking between

60
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:38,220
articles.

61
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:39,220
Yes.

62
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:44,580
Let's set a deadline for keyword research by Tuesday so drafts can start Wednesday.

63
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:45,580
Agreed.

64
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:47,260
Now, timeline.

65
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,420
The launch is three weeks from today.

66
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:52,340
Pre-launch teasers on social start next week.

67
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:56,060
Email campaigns go live two days before official launch.

68
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:57,940
Blogs published mid-week.

69
00:03:57,940 --> 00:04:00,180
Video content ready by launch day.

70
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:03,540
PR outreach begins one day post launch.

71
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:04,500
Excellent.

72
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,660
We should also have daily checkpoints

73
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:09,420
during the final week to confirm all content,

74
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:13,780
graphics, videos, and ad creatives are ready and approved.

75
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:16,640
Yes, and we need clear escalation paths.

76
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:19,020
If anything is delayed, graphic approvals,

77
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:21,100
copy revisions or video editing,

78
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:24,820
we need to know immediately so we can reallocate resources.

79
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:25,780
Agreed.

80
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,420
Let's define risks.

81
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:30,820
First, content delays, emails, blogs,

82
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:32,880
social posts, videos.

83
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:36,620
Second, messaging inconsistencies across channels.

84
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:38,580
Third, technical issues.

85
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,740
Emails not sending, landing pages broken.

86
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:44,620
Fourth, underperforming paid ads.

87
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:48,340
Fifth, negative or unexpected customer feedback.

88
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:51,100
Right, for mitigation, content delays,

89
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:53,620
daily check-ins and deadline enforcement,

90
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:56,400
messaging, centralized review process,

91
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:59,140
technical issues, QA testing of emails,

92
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:01,620
landing pages and social scheduling,

93
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:03,900
paid campaigns, monitored daily

94
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,900
and optimized based on data,

95
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:09,460
feedback, pre-prepared FAQ and support scripts.

96
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:10,380
Perfect.

97
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:15,340
Also, I propose a dedicated Slack channel for campaign coordination.

98
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:19,940
All updates, issues, approvals, and risks are posted there.

99
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:23,460
Each team member tags themselves if they own the task.

100
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:28,020
Yes, this will streamline communication and reduce back and forth emails.

101
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:32,300
Daily updates should be concise, one line per task with status.

102
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,300
Agreed.

103
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:47,860
Now KPIs, email, open rate 35%, CTR 20%, conversions 5%, social, engagement 4%, CTR 2%, reach 50,000

104
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:57,420
plus, blogs, traffic 1,000 views per article, conversions 3%, videos views 2,500 plus, average

105
00:05:57,420 --> 00:06:10,780
watch time 60%, paid ads, CPC under $3, impressions 100,000, CTR 1.5%, PR 5 mentions 80% positive

106
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:11,780
sentiment.

107
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:14,500
Those are ambitious but realistic.

108
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:17,660
I suggest we monitor daily and make adjustments.

109
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:22,860
For example, if CTR is below benchmark, we tweak copy or targeting immediately.

110
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:29,820
Absolutely. Dependencies. Email depends on finalized graphics and copy. Social depends

111
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:35,420
on approved blog links and video content. Paid ads depend on audience targeting being

112
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:39,580
finalized. PR depends on campaign materials ready.

113
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:45,220
Yes, let's map dependencies in a visual timeline. That way everyone sees the critical path

114
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:46,820
in bottlenecks.

115
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:47,820
Good idea.

116
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:49,420
Now, approvals.

117
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:53,020
All content should be finalized two days before launch.

118
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:58,780
Email, social, blogs, videos, and ads all reviewed and approved.

119
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:02,020
Any changes after that require leadership sign off.

120
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,020
Agreed.

121
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:05,500
We should also schedule a pre-launch rehearsal.

122
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:10,540
Test emails, check landing pages, verify links, review social scheduling.

123
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:11,540
Perfect.

124
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:13,140
Now, metrics tracking.

125
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:18,380
I suggest a dashboard with all KPIs updated daily during the launch week.

126
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:25,220
Emails, social, paid ads, and blogs tracked individually with cumulative metrics displayed.

127
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:28,740
Yes, and we should highlight items that fall below benchmarks.

128
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:33,540
Any underperforming channel triggers a quick meeting to assess and adjust strategy.

129
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:39,180
Good. Contingency plans, email issues, resend or adjust schedule.

130
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:42,820
Social issues, reschedule or boost posts.

131
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:47,080
Technical issues redirect traffic, update FAQ.

132
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:51,580
Paid ads under performance optimize targeting and creatives.

133
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:55,220
Negative feedback, pre-prepared response templates.

134
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,220
Excellent.

135
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,340
Finally, post-launch review.

136
00:07:58,340 --> 00:08:01,380
Two weeks after launch, we hold a full retrospective.

137
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:05,460
Review KPIs, lessons learned, feedback from internal teams

138
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,740
and customers, and identify improvements

139
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:09,260
for the next campaign.

140
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:10,060
Agreed.

141
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:12,700
Everything documented in a shared folder.

142
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:18,460
include metrics, notes, screenshots, creative examples, and a summary of lessons learned.

143
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:24,860
Perfect. That ensures institutional knowledge and allows us to scale future campaigns more effectively.

144
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:32,060
All right, let's summarize. Messaging pillars confirmed, channels and owners defined, timeline

145
00:08:32,060 --> 00:08:39,260
and dependencies mapped, risks identified with mitigations, KPIs established, approvals processed

146
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:45,580
defined, dashboards ready, contingencies planned, and post-launch retrospective scheduled.

147
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:51,180
Exactly. I'll draft a recap and share in the Slack channel. Once posted, execution begins

148
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:52,580
according to plan.

149
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:58,260
Perfect. Everyone will have clarity on ownership, deadlines, and escalation. That's what

150
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:00,260
