167
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:18,340
We want to make sure each piece of content,

168
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:21,780
whether it's email, social media, or blog posts,

169
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:23,340
carries that tone.

170
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:26,540
Good point, tone consistency is critical.

171
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:30,660
I want to avoid any disjointed messaging across channels.

172
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:37,740
For example, if email is more formal while social posts are casual, it confuses customers.

173
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:42,340
Exactly. That's why we need clear templates and guidelines for each channel.

174
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:49,180
Subject lines, post captions, graphics, and CTAs all need to adhere to the same principles.

175
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:57,700
On channels, I've mapped out email, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, blog posts, and PR outreach.

176
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:01,700
I want to confirm ownership so that accountability is clear.

177
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:05,300
For social media, I can take LinkedIn and Twitter.

178
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:09,520
I'll handle content creation, scheduling, and engagement monitoring.

179
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:14,420
We can plan Instagram content as well, though we'll need design support for visuals and

180
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:15,420
